course: dictionary
lesson: 2242
title: Words that sound like what they mean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words copy the sound they describe. Crackle is one of them. Say it out loud and you can hear the short, sharp snaps it names. Listening for clues like this helps you work out a new word.
explain: «Then a coal slipped, the fire crackled and sent up a spurt of flame.» A fire making small, sharp sounds fits with the coal slipping and the flame jumping up, so crackled must mean made short, snapping noises. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Crackle is also a noun, a crackle, meaning one of those sounds. It can describe a feeling too: «crackle with excitement» means full of excitement, as if the feeling is fizzing inside you. When a word can mean more than one thing, read the words around it.
fact: To crackle means to make a lot of short, sharp, small sounds.
fact: A crackle is one of these sounds, or a series of them.
fact: Dry wood snaps and pops when it burns, and that crackling is a clear example of sound.
fact: To crackle with something, like excitement or energy, means to be full of it.
fact: Crackled is the past tense and crackling is the present participle, so they show when the sounds happened.
exercise: «Then a coal slipped, the fire crackled and sent up a spurt of flame.» What does crackled mean here? | Glowed in complete silence | Fell slowly onto the floor | Turned very cold and still | *Made short, sharp snapping sounds
exercise: «At first it's fun: twigs crackle, logs trip him.» What do the twigs do? | Grow tall and green | Hide under the logs | *Make short, snapping sounds underfoot | Melt into water
exercise: Ella says, «The room is crackling with excitement.» What does crackling with excitement mean? | Lost in the dark | Very quiet and still | Burning hot like a fire | *Full of excitement
test: Newly hatched clownfish find a reef by its smell and crackling sound. In that sentence, what helps the fish find the reef? | A map drawn by a diver | *Its smell and a crackling sound | A loud song from the seabed | Bright lights from the sun
test: «When enough charge builds up it can jump across a gap as a spark, like the tiny zap from a door handle.» What does crackle mean in «the crackle of a jumper pulled off in the dark»? | A cold, wet patch | *A short, sharp, snapping sound | A bright, steady glow | A long, quiet hum
exam: In «each crackle is a tiny spark», what is a crackle? | A long, quiet hum | A steady, glowing light | A cold, wet patch | *A short, sharp sound
